  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Human Security through Community-Based, Community-Led Solutions in Conflict-Affected Repatriation Areas in Ukraine and Strengthening Consular Services of Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to improve human security in conflict-affected regions of return in Ukraine through implementing area-based and community-driven solutions, as well as strengthening consular services for Ukrainian nationals. The project will place a particular emphasis on empowering women and other vulnerable or marginalized groups, including internally displaced persons (IDPs), youth, older persons, persons with disabilities, survivors of human trafficking, gender-based violence (GBV), exploitation, and other forms of abuse, and war veterans. The project will prioritize activities that support community-level winter preparedness and response. By linking humanitarian assistance to peace and development programming, the project aims to address mid-term needs of conflict-affected populations, thereby reducing their long-term dependency on aid. The project will focus on areas of high return that are conducive to community stabilization programming, which tentatively include Kyiv City, Kyiv Oblast, Chernihiv Oblast, and Poltava Oblast. IOM will target a total of six communities in these regions.</narrative>
  </description>
